    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered pipeline for `POST /api/owners`, as wired in `owners.POST.yml`. Every step runs under a single write transaction (`govern: [ transaction ]`), so the whole thing commits once at the end.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. Without that role the request is denied (handled by the `AuthorizationDeniedException` escalation) and no step runs.\n\n## Steps in execution order\n\n1. **NormalizeAddress** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Binds the request body (`@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`; this is the **only** body-bind in the pipeline) and normalizes `address` via `AddressNormalizer`: trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, and expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`. `null`/blank \u2192 empty string. Republishes the request for later steps.\n   - Note: the body is bound **without `@Valid`**, so the DTO's bean-validation annotations are *not* enforced at the endpoint \u2014 all validation below is the explicit code shown.\n\n2. **RequireOwnerFields** *(validation)* \u2014 Rejects if any of `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` is null/blank (tested *after* address normalization). Throws `MissingOwnerFieldsException`.\n\n3. **ValidatePostcode** *(validation)* \u2014 Optional `postcode`: absent/blank is accepted. If present it must be exactly 4 digits, and for a city with a known region (`Locality`/`PostcodeRanges`: NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) it must fall in range. Malformed/out-of-range \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (400). Unknown region \u2192 any 4 digits accepted.\n\n4. **NormalizeTelephone** *(validation + side-effect)* \u2014 Normalizes `telephone` to E.164 (`TelephoneE164`): strips spaces/dashes/brackets; keeps `+`/country code or assumes `+61` and drops one leading `0`; requires 8\u201315 digits, and enforces national length per country (`+61`\u21929 digits, `+1`\u219210). Writes normalized value back. Invalid \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (400).\n\n5. **NormalizeEmail** *(validation + side-effect)* \u2014 Optional `email`: absent/blank left untouched. If present, must match a basic syntactic pattern (else `InvalidEmailException`, 400), otherwise trimmed and lower-cased and written back.\n\n6. **RejectDuplicateOwner** *(validation)* \u2014 Scans all existing owners; if the request's normalized telephone equals any existing owner's telephone (normalized to E.164 for comparison), throws `DuplicateIdentityException` (409).\n   - \u26a0\ufe0f Discrepancy worth flagging: the class Javadoc describes matching on a composite `IdentityKey` (telephone + email + household), but the **actual code only compares normalized telephone**. Email/household play no part in the real duplicate check.\n\n7. **RejectCityAtCapacity** *(validation)* \u2014 Counts existing owners in the same city (matched case-insensitively, whitespace-collapsed). If \u2265 `CITY_CAPACITY` (50) \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (409).\n\n8. **RejectOverDailyLimit** *(validation)* \u2014 Computes the effective registration day (request value or today, rolled off weekends to Monday via `BusinessDay`). If \u2265 `DAILY_LIMIT` (100) owners already have that `registrationDate` \u2192 `DailyLimitExceededException` (429).\n\n9. **BuildOwner** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Maps the DTO to an `Owner` entity via `OwnerMapper`, then sets `registrationDate` to the effective date adjusted forward off any weekend (`BusinessDay.adjust`).\n\n10. **AssignCustomerCode** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Sets `customerCode` = `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`: first 3 letters of city (upper), first 3 of last name (upper), and a per-city 4-digit sequence = (count of existing owners in that city) + 1.\n\n11. **AssignMembershipNumber** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Sets `membershipNumber` = `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, where YY is the last two digits of the adjusted registration year.\n\n12. **CountNamesakes** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Sets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n\n13. **AssignMembershipLevel** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Sets `membershipLevel`: starts at 1, +1 if email present, +1 if `namesakeCount == 0`, capped at 3.\n\n14. **CountHousehold** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Sets `householdSize` = 1 + existing owners in the same household (same normalized last name **and** normalized address).\n\n15. **FlagBulkSignup** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Sets `bulkSignupWarning = true` if strictly more than `BULK_SIGNUP_THRESHOLD` (80) owners already exist for the adjusted registration day, else false.\n\n16. **SaveOwner** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Persists the owner (`ownerRepository.save`), assigning its id.\n\n17. **AuditOwnerCreated** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Logs an audit line to the `AUDIT` logger with id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel.\n\n18. **RespondWithOwnerCreated** *(side-effect / response)* \u2014 Maps to `OwnerDto` and sends **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and the DTO body.\n\n## Summary\n- **Validations (can reject), in order:** required fields \u2192 postcode format/range \u2192 telephone E.164 validity \u2192 email syntax \u2192 duplicate telephone (409) \u2192 city capacity (409) \u2192 daily limit (429).\n- **Side-effects, in order:** address normalization \u2192 telephone normalization \u2192 email normalization \u2192 build entity \u2192 weekend-adjusted registration date \u2192 customerCode \u2192 membershipNumber \u2192 namesakeCount \u2192 membershipLevel \u2192 householdSize \u2192 bulkSignupWarning \u2192 persist (id assigned) \u2192 audit log \u2192 201 response.\n\nAll under one transaction that commits only after the final step succeeds; any thrown exception aborts before commit."
